# LOST LINKS: the route proof. From a new game the demo player (the "bot"
# query) plays the whole world by real button presses: it swings the aim
# with the d-pad, holds A and lets go at the power it wants, holds A
# again to brake and taps B to jump off sand. Its way round is
# lostlinks_route.h; each stroke is chosen by trying every swing with the game's own rolling rules. It finds
# every iron, stray, scorecrow, ability and piece, sets the Star Pin, lights
# the plates and beats the Brass Badger: every goal, in one game.
seed 18
game lostlinks
wait 5
press A
botuntil abilities & 1 20000
expect irons >= 10
botuntil bot_wp >= 34 30000
expect abilities & 2
botuntil bot_wp >= 45 30000
expect abilities & 4
botuntil bot_wp >= 55 30000
expect abilities == 15
botuntil pieces == 15 20000
botuntil placed == 1 20000
botuntil won == 1 30000
expect irons == 20
expect strays == 8
expect crows == 10
expect pins == 10
expect goals == 7
expect state == 6
